From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 17:21:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] code_block: split a block into a shell and a body

Most of a bundle's functions never run, yet each keeps its constants, binding locators,
handlers, IC names, source map and global tables resident (about 540 B a block, 25 MiB on
a large app). Moving those out needs them behind one door: the shell keeps what making a
function object, printing its source and running its bytecode read (flags, length, this
mode, name, toString span, bytecode), and everything else goes in a `CodeBody` reached
through `body()`. The toString span moves out of `SourceInfo` into the shell, its only
reader. No behaviour changes.
